---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Layout title="Legal, Governance & Policies">

  <main class="py-8">
    <Hero 
      title="Legal, Governance & Policies" 
      description="This page outlines Impact Orbit Creative Group’s legal framework, governance approach, and integrated management system, including links to our core policies."
    />

    <section class="py-16 bg-white dark:bg-secondary-500">
      <div class="container-custom">
        <article class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-4xl mx-auto">

          <p class="mb-8 text-white dark:text-white">
            <strong>Last Updated:</strong> 30 July 2025
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">1. Legal Entity and Scope</h2>
          <p class="mb-6">
            <strong>Impact Orbit Creative Group Ltd</strong> (“Impact Orbit”, “we”, “our”, or “us”) is a private limited company registered in England and Wales (Company No. 15207389).
          </p>

          <address class="not-italic mb-8">
            DOCK – Space City<br />
            75 Exploration Drive<br />
            Leicester, LE4 5NU<br />
            United Kingdom
          </address>

          <p class="mb-8">
            This page applies to Impact Orbit Creative Group Ltd and its associated brands, initiatives, and digital platforms, including <strong>Green Orbit Space Communications & PR</strong>, unless otherwise stated.
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">2. Governance and Accountability</h2>
          <p class="mb-6">
            Impact Orbit operates with a governance model designed to support transparency, accountability, and responsible decision-making across commercial, environmental, and social domains.
          </p>

          <ul class="mb-8 list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
            <li>Clear executive accountability for legal, ethical, and sustainability matters.</li>
            <li>Documented policies and procedures aligned with applicable UK law and recognised international standards.</li>
            <li>Risk-based decision-making informed by data, materiality, and proportionality.</li>
            <li>Regular review of policies to reflect changes in regulation, industry practice, and organisational growth.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">3. Integrated Management System (IMS)</h2>
          <p class="mb-6">
            Impact Orbit maintains an <strong>Integrated Management System (IMS)</strong> that brings together governance, risk management, data protection, information security, sustainability, and quality practices into a single, coherent framework.
          </p>

          <p class="mb-6">
            Our IMS is designed to align with the intent and principles of recognised standards, including:
          </p>

          <ul class="mb-8 list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
            <li>ISO 9001 (Quality Management)</li>
            <li>ISO/IEC 27001 (Information Security Management)</li>
            <li>ISO 14001 (Environmental Management)</li>
            <li>ISO 22301 (Business Continuity)</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="mb-8">
            While certification status may vary by area, our policies, controls, and operating procedures are structured to support continual improvement, auditability, and regulatory compliance.
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">4. Core Policies</h2>
          <p class="mb-6">
            The following policies form the foundation of Impact Orbit’s legal and operational framework. These apply across our websites, services, and client engagements unless otherwise stated.
          </p>

          <ul class="mb-10 list-disc list-inside space-y-3">
            <li>
              <a href="/privacy-policy" class="text-accent-500 hover:underline">
                Privacy Policy
              </a>
              – How we collect, use, and protect personal data.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/cookie-policy" class="text-accent-500 hover:underline">
                Cookie Policy
              </a>
              – How cookies and similar technologies are used across our sites.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/information-security-policy" class="text-accent-500 hover:underline">
                Information Security Policy
              </a>
              – Our approach to protecting information assets and managing cyber risk.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/data-protection-policy" class="text-accent-500 hover:underline">
                Data Protection Policy
              </a>
              – Internal controls supporting compliance with UK GDPR and data protection law.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/sustainability-policy" class="text-accent-500 hover:underline">
                Sustainability & Environmental Policy
              </a>
              – Our commitment to responsible, sustainable practices in the space sector.
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/code-of-conduct" class="text-accent-500 hover:underline">
                Code of Conduct & Ethics
              </a>
              – Expected standards of behaviour for staff, partners, and suppliers.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">5. Risk Management</h2>
          <p class="mb-6">
            Risks to our business, clients, and stakeholders are identified, assessed, and managed through our IMS using a proportionate, risk-based approach.
          </p>

          <ul class="mb-8 list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
            <li>Information security and data protection risks.</li>
            <li>Operational and delivery risks.</li>
            <li>Legal and regulatory compliance risks.</li>
            <li>Environmental and sustainability-related risks.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">6. Third Parties and Suppliers</h2>
          <p class="mb-8">
            Impact Orbit works with carefully selected suppliers and partners. Where relevant, third parties are subject to contractual obligations covering confidentiality, data protection, and security, aligned with our internal policies and IMS controls.
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">7. Legal Compliance</h2>
          <p class="mb-8">
            We aim to comply with all applicable UK legislation, including (but not limited to) company law, data protection law, consumer protection law, and electronic communications regulations. Compliance obligations are reviewed regularly as part of our governance processes.
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">8. Policy Review and Updates</h2>
          <p class="mb-8">
            This page and the linked policies may be updated periodically to reflect changes in law, standards, or organisational practices. The most current versions will always be published on our website.
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-10 mb-4">9. Contact and Further Information</h2>
          <p class="mb-6">
            For questions regarding our governance framework, policies, or Integrated Management System, please contact us:
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mb-6">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">
              Contact Us
            </a>
          </div>

          <address class="not-italic text-sm mb-8">
            Impact Orbit Creative Group Ltd<br />
            Email: <a href="mailto:hello@impactorbit.co" class="text-accent-500 hover:underline">hello@impactorbit.co</a><br />
            Phone: +44 116 483 0155
          </address>

        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

</Layout>